            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0817" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg723"/>

                <head>No. 468.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 14, 1887</date>.
                        (Received May 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    translation of Mr. Mariscal’s reply to my several notes concerning the complaint
                    of Messrs. F. Alexandre &amp; Sons regarding the rebate of duties accorded to
                    the Spanish Transatlantic Mail Steam-ship Company. You will see that the
                    Government of Mexico justifies its action, denies that Messrs. Alexandre have
                    any just cause of complaint, and, in effect, though not in terms, refuses to
                    give any relief.</p>
                <p>Copy of the note will follow soon. I did not wish to delay this.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. C. Manning.</hi></signed></closer>





